--TEST--
`Core\Zip` reads and extracts an entry 64 folders deep and refuses one 65 deep before anything is written, because each level of an extraction costs a walk of every level above it — `rule:security/path-scope-canonicalise-then-prefix`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Zip::extract
class Archive
{
    // An archive with one empty file, stored uncompressed. An empty file has
    // the checksum 0, so every field is known without computing one.
    public static function one(string $name): bytes
    {
        bytes $spelled = $name as bytes;
        uint $length = Core\Bytes::length($spelled);
        bytes $local = Core\Bytes::join([
            Core\Bytes::pack('VvvvvvVVVvv', 0x04034b50, 20, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, $length, 0),
            $spelled,
        ]);
        bytes $record = Core\Bytes::join([
            Core\Bytes::pack('VvvvvvvVVVvvvvvVV', 0x02014b50, 20, 20, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, $length, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
            $spelled,
        ]);
        return Core\Bytes::join([
            $local,
            $record,
            Core\Bytes::pack('VvvvvVVv', 0x06054b50, 0, 0, 1, 1, Core\Bytes::length($record), Core\Bytes::length($local), 0),
        ]);
    }
}

// The bound includes 64: a file under 64 folders is listed and extracted.
string $deepest = Core\Str::repeat("d/", 64) . "f.txt";
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Zip::entries(Archive::one($deepest))), "\n";
echo Core\Zip::extract(Archive::one($deepest), "out"), "\n";
echo Core\IO::exists(Core\Path::join("out", $deepest)) ? "written\n" : "missing\n";

// One folder more is refused when the archive is read, so every member refuses
// it. The message shows only the start of the name.
string $tooDeep = Core\Str::repeat("d/", 65) . "f.txt";
try {
    Core\Zip::entries(Archive::one($tooDeep));
    echo "listed\n";
} catch (ParseError $refused) {
    echo $refused->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Core\Zip::extract(Archive::one($tooDeep), "never");
    echo "extracted\n";
} catch (ParseError $refused) {
    echo "extract: ParseError\n";
}
echo Core\IO::isDir("never") ? "never: created\n" : "never: not created\n";

// A folder entry counts its own level, so 65 folders is refused as well.
try {
    Core\Zip::entries(Archive::one(Core\Str::repeat("d/", 65)));
    echo "listed\n";
} catch (ParseError $refused) {
    echo "folder: ParseError\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
write = ["."]
--EXPECT--
1
1
written
Core\Zip will not read an entry: it nests 65 folders and an archive may nest at most 64, because extracting a folder costs a walk of every folder above it: "d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/d/…".
extract: ParseError
never: not created
folder: ParseError
